That's how I deal with her.  For any covetous monster, I end up waiting
a knight's move away from the stairway they're hogging, so that I can
then step (or jump, if I'm a knight or appropriately booted) towards the
stairwell as soon as they hop off it to attack.  So I just have to
approach that spot while avoiding the 8 line-of-attack directions.

My problem with this approach is that it means she gets three
consecutive attack rounds in with me moving, not attacking or healing,
in between them.  It's a tough decision whether to quaff the !oFH and
risk missing the chance at the stairway.

It might be preferable to wake her up from the stairway, if at all
possible.  Horn?  Fumble boots?

